item.text:
In MOOS apps, mail registration should happen in `OnConnectToServer()`, because reconnecting to the MOOSDB can drop prior subscriptions. `OnStartUp()` is for reading config and initial setup; it may run only once, so registrations done only there can be lost after a reconnect.

Correct pattern conceptually:

```cpp
bool Odometry::OnStartUp()
{
  // Read mission/config params here.
  return true;
}

bool Odometry::OnConnectToServer()
{
  Register("NAV_X", 0);
  Register("NAV_Y", 0);
  return true;
}
```

Often this is wrapped in a helper:

```cpp
void Odometry::RegisterVariables()
{
  Register("NAV_X", 0);
  Register("NAV_Y", 0);
}

bool Odometry::OnStartUp()
{
  RegisterVariables(); // optional initial registration
  return true;
}

bool Odometry::OnConnectToServer()
{
  RegisterVariables(); // required for reconnects
  return true;
}
```

The important rule: registrations must be performed from `OnConnectToServer()` so they are reissued every time the app connects or reconnects to the MOOSDB.
